@* The snapshot guard: a query string carries the answered count it was run over; when the batch
   now has another count the note says so, since every count in the view may differ from what a
   lead recorded. Parameter-driven, no services. *@
@if (Expected != Actual)
{
    <p class="note">This query was run over @Expected answered results; the batch now has @Actual. The counts below are over the batch as it is now.</p>
}

@code {
    [Parameter] public int Expected { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public int Actual { get; set; }
}
